# tr808 — the SAME snare at two velocities, for the §J9 velocity→noisiness A/B (plan item 1.3).
#
# The trick is that the cart's own presets already give us both cases, so nothing has to be hand-edited:
#   PLANET ROCK  accent "x.......x......."  ·  SD row "....x.......x..."   → snares NEVER accented (boost 0)
#   BOOM BAP     accent "....x.......x..."  ·  SD row "....x.......x..."   → snares ALWAYS accented (boost 2)
# So this plays ~2.5s of PLANET ROCK, presses RIGHT four times to reach BOOM BAP (preset 4), and plays
# ~3.8s of that. One render contains an unaccented and an accented snare under otherwise identical code.
#
# That makes the A/B self-verifying, which is the point:
#   node tools/ab-render.js tr808 --file runtime/tr808.h --set tr808_snare_dyn=0,1 \
#        --script tools/clips/tr808/02-snare-soft-vs-accent.script --frames 400
#   node tools/wav-envelope.js <wav> 100 --from 0.2 --to 2.4   # PLANET ROCK — MUST be identical (boost 0)
#   node tools/wav-envelope.js <wav> 100 --from 3.2 --to 6.4   # BOOM BAP    — should differ (boost 2)
# If the first region differs, the tilt is leaking into soft hits and something is wrong.
#
# Tempo differs between the presets (126 vs 90 BPM) — that is the presets' own data, not a variable here.
down 150 RIGHT
up 152 RIGHT
down 156 RIGHT
up 158 RIGHT
down 162 RIGHT
up 164 RIGHT
down 168 RIGHT
up 170 RIGHT
